  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>The Burmese Dwarf Stickleback or Paradox Fish, Indostomus paradoxus, is a tiny species. It grows only 2-3 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>It originates from the northern parts of Burma.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>The species should be kept in single species tanks; so-called nano-tanks fit perfectly.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>The species is best kept at room temperature (18-22°C). The water should be medium hard to hard and the pH should be around 6.5 – 8.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>The Paradox Fish feeds exclusively on small live food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>Indostomus are very peaceful towards conspecifics, but they are too weak to compete with other species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>Females become larger than males, otherwise the sexes are difficult to distinguish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>It has been bred occasionally. The Burmese Dwarf Stickleback breeds in caves such as bamboo stems.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/20-sticklebacks/indostomus-paradoxus-4/",
      "html": "<p>Despite its diminutiveness the fish is rather hardy and can live for a long time in aquaria.</p><p>Etymology: Indostomus means roughly \"with a very tiny mouth\"; paradoxus means \"very strange, paradox\".</p>"
    }
  ],
